---
// src/pages/bucknell/index.astro  →  arizvi.com/bucknell
// Hub for the Bucknell business analytics search: how I teach, the courses, and classes to try.
// Each course has its own page. Not linked from the nav; sends noindex.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import CurriculumMap from '../../components/CurriculumMap.astro';
import { arrows, courses, students } from '../../data/bucknell';

const principles = [
  ['Build the course backwards from the outcome.', 'I start each course from where it fits in the program, where it falls in the students\' path through their degree, and where they\'ll use it afterwards. Then I set what students should be able to do by the end of term.'],
  ['Personalize within a defined structure.', 'Everyone learns the same methods. Within that, I adjust to the cohort in front of me. In the sophomore course, each student chose a second skill to learn alongside their core project.'],
  ['Learn on real problems.', 'Students understand a problem best when they work in the setting that produces it, so my projects send them there, to users well beyond their class lists, from pharmacists to fruit wholesalers.'],
  ['Test the teaching itself.', 'I compare course designs across cohorts, share the results with colleagues teaching the same students, and carry the stronger design into the next term.'],
];
---
<Base title="Bucknell" description="The courses Ali Rizvi would teach in Bucknell's Analytics & Operations Management department, and how he teaches them." noindex>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="intro-grid">
      <div class="text">
        <p class="label">Bucknell · Analytics &amp; Operations Management</p>
        <h1>Teaching analytics at Bucknell</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="photo"><img src="/media/headshot.jpg" alt="Ali Rizvi" width="400" height="500" /></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <Section label="How I teach" id="approach">
    <ol class="principles">
      {principles.map(([head, line]) => <li><strong>{head}</strong> {line}</li>)}
    </ol>
    <p class="muted principles-note">14 course sections of 6 courses at Waterloo between 2021 and 2024, over 700 students, up to 4 sections and 180 students in a term, in person, hybrid and online. 3 colleagues have adopted a course I built. My years at PwC, EY, Morgan Stanley and Amazon give students worked examples. The classes on the course pages use small invented businesses, so the numbers can be checked, and each course has a full pack: the syllabus, every week, the labs or deliverables, the rubrics, and a sample exam where the course has one. More on the <a href="/teaching/">Teaching</a> page.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="The courses" id="courses">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>In my letter I said I'd teach ANOP 102, ANOP 330 and ANOP 400, for the posting's 3 areas: spreadsheet modeling and analysis, machine learning, and project-based capstone courses. ANOP 302, the other spreadsheet modeling course in the 2026-27 catalogue, is here too.</p>
    </div></div>
    <CurriculumMap />
    <ul class="rows bk-wide">
      {courses.map((c) => (
        <li class="grid">
          <div class="label">{c.code}<br />{c.where}</div>
          <div class="body">
            <a class="title" href={`/bucknell/${c.slug}/`}>{c.title}&nbsp;→</a>
            <p>{arrows(c.line)}</p>
            <p class="who"><span class="label">Students</span>{students(c)}</p>
            <p class="sample"><a href={`/bucknell/${c.slug}/`}>{c.sample}</a></p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;"><strong>New electives.</strong> I'd develop 2, offered first as ANOP 315 special topics. AI for business decisions takes the manager's seat: when to hand a decision to a model, how to check its work, and how to keep each decision auditable. Evaluating AI systems has students bring a system of their own and design a study on it with people in the loop.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Advising" id="advising">
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p>I advise the way I teach, one student at a time. I built that practice mentoring more than 30 people at Morgan Stanley and Amazon, carried it into individual meetings with every student in every course I taught, and still mentor students I taught in 2021. Two students from my graduate HCI course are first authors on a paper under preparation for DIS 2027, with me as senior author. At Bucknell, ANOP 310 independent studies and ANOP 390 honors work are where I'd bring undergraduates into applied analytics research.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Try a class" id="try">
    <ul class="rows bk-wide">
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 3</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#pivot">Clean it before you count it&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>A coffee cart's sales export, a pivot table, and 3 fixes that change who's on top.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 6</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#breakeven">How wrong can the forecast be?&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>A taco truck's profit for every price and every volume at once, and the breakeven that moves with the assumptions.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 8</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#llm">An LLM gives you probabilities&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>How an LLM picks its next word, and how a decision model should use what it says.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 11</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#regression">One weekend flips the slope&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>12 weeks of ad spend and sales, a fitted line, and the one weekend that decides whether the ads pay.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 330<br />Week 8</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-330/#threshold">The most accurate cutoff earns nothing&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>1,000 customers, 100 about to cancel, and a retention offer. Watch accuracy and money pull in opposite directions.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 330<br />Week 4</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-330/#overfit">The model that memorised the past&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>Fit a curve to 16 days of sales, pick the degree you'd ship, then reveal the 8 days it never saw.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 302<br />Week 12</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-302/#try">Price an option by simulation&nbsp;→</a>
          <p>Simulate stock paths and watch the estimate close in on Black-Scholes.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>
</Base>
